Block: nngp_gaussian_gibbs_block
Version: 0.1.0
Date: 2026-06-30
Title: Nearest-Neighbor Gaussian Process spatial regression sampler
Description: Fits Bayesian Gaussian spatial regression with a Nearest-Neighbor
 Gaussian Process (NNGP) random effect, y_i ~ N(x_i' beta + w_i, tau^2), where the
 spatial effects follow the sparse NNGP approximation w_i | w_N(i) ~ N(b_i' w_N(i),
 f_i) built from an exponential covariance sigma^2 exp(-phi d) over each location's m
 nearest neighbors (KD-tree neighbor search). The coefficients beta take a
 weakly-informative Gaussian prior, the nugget tau^2 and partial sill sigma^2
 Inverse-Gamma priors, and the decay phi a domain-scaled uniform prior. Replaces the
 dense n-by-n GP covariance with a sparse neighbor-based approximation, scaling
 Gaussian-process spatial modeling to large point-referenced datasets. The effects w
 (block sparse-Cholesky draw), coefficients beta and nugget tau^2 are sampled by
 conjugate Gibbs steps; the partial sill sigma^2 and decay phi are updated jointly (a
 sigma^2-marginalized slice on phi then a conjugate sigma^2 draw), and an exact
 parameter-expansion level shift improves intercept mixing. Datta, Banerjee, Finley
 and Gelfand (2016) <doi:10.1080/01621459.2015.1044091>; Finley et al. (2019)
 <doi:10.1080/10618600.2018.1537924>.
Author: Jungang Zou
Maintainer: Jungang Zou <jz3183@cumc.columbia.edu>
License: GPL-3.0-or-later
EngineKind: mcmc
ConstraintKinds: none
RoutingKey: large point-referenced spatial Gaussian process
SelectWhen: Large-scale spatial regression with Gaussian-process random effects on
 point-referenced data
